EXPERIMENT 10
PL/SQL Programming — conditional blocks, exceptions, procedures, functions, triggers, cursors

EXPECTED OUTPUT / RESULT

Conditional IF-ELSIF for employee 102 (ALLEN, salary 15000):
ALLEN: Grade B

Searched CASE bonus for employee 103 (SALESMAN, salary 12500):
Bonus: 1250

Predefined exception for employee number 999:
No employee with that number.

OUT-parameter procedure for employee 104:
JONES earns 29750

IN OUT procedure with input 7:
Result: 49

The trigger trg_check_sal rejects a negative salary with application error -20010. The audit trigger records DML changes in EMP_AUDIT. The implicit cursor reports the number of rows updated; the explicit cursor prints employees ordered by salary descending.

The manual explicitly gives “JONES earns 29750” as an expected output. Other output formatting depends on SQL*Plus settings.
